<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>WinExe</OutputType>
    <!--
      跟 WPF 版本（net10.0-windows）最大的区别：这里是纯 net10.0，不带 "-windows" 后缀
      （选 net10.0 而非更低的 net8.0 的原因见下一段注释）。Avalonia 本身就是跨平台 UI
      框架，具体平台实现（Win32/X11/Wayland/macOS）由 Avalonia.Desktop 在运行时根据当前
      OS 自动选择，不需要也不应该把 TargetFramework 锁定成某个平台专属 TFM——这也是这次
      把 WPF Demo 换成 Avalonia Demo 的收益之一：win-x64/linux-x64 两个 RID 共用
      同一份 TFM，不用再像 WPF 项目那样为了 PlatformTarget/RuntimeIdentifier 的兼容性写
      一堆条件判断（参见已删除的 SevenZipLite.WpfDemo.csproj 历史记录）。

      The biggest difference from the old WPF project (net10.0-windows): this is plain
      net10.0, no "-windows" suffix (see the next comment block for why net10.0 rather
      than the lower net8.0). Avalonia is a cross-platform UI framework by design; the
      concrete platform backend (Win32/X11/Wayland/macOS) is selected by
      Avalonia.Desktop at runtime based on the current OS — there's no need (and no
      benefit) to pin TargetFramework to a platform-specific TFM. This is also one of
      the payoffs of replacing the WPF demo with this Avalonia demo: win-x64/
      linux-x64 share the exact same TFM, with no need for the PlatformTarget/
      RuntimeIdentifier compatibility conditionals the old WPF project needed (see the
      now-deleted SevenZipLite.WpfDemo.csproj's history).

      选 net10.0（而不是库支持的最低 TFM net8.0）：跟仓库里其余 samples/tests 项目
      （SevenZipLite.SelfTest / SevenZipLite.Tests / SevenZipLite.MauiDemo）保持一致——
      本项目引用的 SevenZipLite.SelfTest 只单一目标 net10.0（它的定位是"被各个 Demo
      共享的自检用例代码"，不是要打包分发的库，没有多目标的必要），net8.0 会直接导致
      NU1201 还原失败。Avalonia + Native AOT 组合官方样例虽然多数用 net8.0，但 net9.0/
      net10.0 同样被官方验证支持（见 Avalonia 官方仓库关于 NativeAOT 的 issue/讨论），
      不存在 net10.0 下 Avalonia AOT 不可用的问题。

      Targets net10.0 (rather than net8.0, the library's lowest supported TFM): kept
      consistent with every other samples/tests project in this repo (SevenZipLite.
      SelfTest / SevenZipLite.Tests / SevenZipLite.MauiDemo). This project references
      SevenZipLite.SelfTest, which only targets net10.0 (its job is to be shared
      self-test case code across the demos, not a library meant for redistribution, so
      multi-targeting it buys nothing) — targeting net8.0 here would simply fail restore
      with NU1201. While most official Avalonia + Native AOT samples use net8.0, net9.0/
      net10.0 are equally officially supported (see Avalonia's own NativeAOT issues/
      discussions) — there's no Avalonia-AOT limitation specific to net10.0.
    -->
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>SevenZipLite.AvaloniaDemo</RootNamespace>
    <BuiltInComInteropSupport>true</BuiltInComInteropSupport>
    <ApplicationManifest>app.manifest</ApplicationManifest>
    <AvaloniaUseCompiledBindingsByDefault>true</AvaloniaUseCompiledBindingsByDefault>

    <!--
      本 Demo 跟 WPF 版本一样完全不用 {Binding ...} / DataContext / MVVM，所有控件都是
      x:Name 具名引用 + 代码后置直接读写属性、挂事件处理器——这不是"偷懒"，而是刻意选择：
      本项目的定位是"验证 SevenZipLite 类库在真实 GUI 应用里能否正常工作"，不是 MVVM 框架
      的示范项目，用最朴素的代码后置方式能让读者的注意力完全集中在 SevenZipLite 的调用上。
      顺带的好处是：没有 {Binding} 就没有反射型绑定，Native AOT 发布天然不会在这方面产生
      任何裁剪/AOT 警告（上面 AvaloniaUseCompiledBindingsByDefault 是双重保险，万一以后
      有人加了 {Binding} 语法，也会被编译期强制要求写成可裁剪安全的编译型绑定）。

      This demo uses no {Binding ...} / DataContext / MVVM at all, same as the old WPF
      version — every control is wired via a named x:Name reference and plain
      code-behind property access / event handlers. That's a deliberate choice, not
      laziness: this project's purpose is to verify the SevenZipLite library works
      correctly in a real GUI app, not to showcase an MVVM framework, and the plainest
      possible code-behind style keeps the reader's attention entirely on the
      SevenZipLite calls. A side benefit: no {Binding} means no reflection-based
      bindings, so the Native AOT publish naturally produces zero trimming/AOT warnings
      on that front (AvaloniaUseCompiledBindingsByDefault above is a belt-and-braces
      safety net — if anyone adds {Binding} syntax later, the compiler will force it to
      be a trim-safe compiled binding instead of a reflection-based one).
    -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- ==================== Native AOT 发布开关 / Native AOT publish switch ==================== -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      跟 src/SevenZipLite/SevenZipLite.csproj 的 IsAotCompatible 不是一回事：那个只是
      "编译期静态分析"开关，这里的 PublishAot 才是真正在 `dotnet publish` 时触发 Native
      AOT 编译、产出不依赖 .NET 运行时的原生可执行文件。本项目能打开这个开关、且
      `dotnet publish -p:PublishAot=true` 零警告通过，依据有二：
        1) SevenZipLite 类库本身已验证 AOT 兼容（见 src/SevenZipLite/SevenZipLite.csproj
           的注释与 tests/SevenZipLite.AotSmokeTest）；
        2) 本 Demo 不使用 {Binding}/MVVM（见上面的注释），Avalonia 侧唯一的 AOT 风险点
           （反射型绑定）被从源头上排除。
      不按 Configuration 区分（没有写 Condition="'$(Configuration)'=='Release'"）：
      微软官方指导是 PublishAot 不应该按构建配置区分（见 .NET MAUI Native AOT 文档），
      因为裁剪相关的功能开关要在所有配置下保持一致，代码行为才不会出现"Debug 正常、
      Release 跑不起来"的不一致；真正只在"发布"时才会生效（`dotnet build`/`dotnet run`
      不受影响，本地日常开发体验不变）。

      Distinct from src/SevenZipLite/SevenZipLite.csproj's IsAotCompatible: that one is
      only a compile-time static-analysis opt-in. PublishAot here is what actually
      triggers Native AOT compilation during `dotnet publish`, producing a native
      executable with no .NET runtime dependency. This project can safely turn it on
      (and `dotnet publish -p:PublishAot=true` passes with zero warnings) for two
      reasons: 1) the SevenZipLite library itself is already AOT-verified (see
      SevenZipLite.csproj's comments and tests/SevenZipLite.AotSmokeTest); 2) this demo
      uses no {Binding}/MVVM (see above), eliminating Avalonia's main AOT risk
      (reflection-based bindings) at the source. Not conditioned on Configuration
      (no Condition="'$(Configuration)'=='Release'"): Microsoft's official guidance is
      that PublishAot shouldn't vary by build configuration (see the .NET MAUI Native
      AOT docs), because trimming-related feature switches need to stay consistent
      across configurations so code behavior doesn't silently diverge between Debug and
      Release. It only actually takes effect when publishing — `dotnet build`/`dotnet
      run` are unaffected, so everyday local development is unchanged.
      注意：`PublishAot=true` 对所有 RID 一视同仁地打开，但 win-x86 用这个开关发布会直接
      失败（`NETSDK1203: Ahead-of-time compilation is not supported for the target
      runtime identifier 'win-x86'.`）——这是 .NET Native AOT 的硬限制（Windows 上只支持
      x64/arm64，从未支持过 32 位），不是本项目能绕开的问题，所以本仓库的 CI
      （`.github/workflows/release.yml` 的 `publish-avalonia` job）只对 win-x64 和
      linux-x64 两个 RID 做发布，不含 win-x86。

      Note: `PublishAot=true` applies uniformly to every RID, but publishing win-x86
      with it fails outright (`NETSDK1203: Ahead-of-time compilation is not supported
      for the target runtime identifier 'win-x86'.`) — this is a hard .NET Native AOT
      limitation (Windows only ever supported x64/arm64, never 32-bit), not something
      this project can work around, so this repo's CI (the `publish-avalonia` job in
      `.github/workflows/release.yml`) only publishes win-x64 and linux-x64, not win-x86.
    -->
    <PublishAot>true</PublishAot>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <AvaloniaResource Include="Assets\**" Condition="Exists('Assets')" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia" Version="12.1.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Desktop" Version="12.1.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Themes.Fluent" Version="12.1.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Fonts.Inter" Version="12.1.3" />
    <!--
      本项目没有引用 Avalonia.Diagnostics（F12 开发者工具）：这个包目前还停留在 11.3.x
      版本线，尚未随 Avalonia 核心包一起发布 12.x 版本（截至本项目编写时，nuget.org 上
      Avalonia/Avalonia.Desktop/Avalonia.Themes.Fluent 都已是 12.1.3，Avalonia.Diagnostics
      最新仍是 11.3.22），版本不匹配会导致还原失败。它本身也只是开发期辅助工具，不影响
      应用功能或本项目要验证的 Native AOT 发布，所以直接不引用，而不是想办法凑一个
      能用的版本组合。

      This project does not reference Avalonia.Diagnostics (the F12 dev tools overlay):
      that package is still on the 11.3.x version line and hasn't shipped a 12.x release
      alongside the core Avalonia packages (as of writing, Avalonia/Avalonia.Desktop/
      Avalonia.Themes.Fluent are all at 12.1.3 on nuget.org, while Avalonia.Diagnostics'
      latest is still 11.3.22) — referencing it would cause a version-mismatch restore
      failure. It's also just a development-time convenience tool that doesn't affect
      app functionality or the Native AOT publish this project exists to verify, so it's
      simply omitted rather than forcing together a working version combination.
    -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\SevenZipLite\SevenZipLite.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\tests\SevenZipLite.SelfTest\SevenZipLite.SelfTest.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    原生库分发策略：跟旧 WPF Demo 的思路一致（复制到输出目录根，供
    [LibraryImport("7zlite")] 的默认探测规则找到），但选择依据从 PlatformTarget（WPF 只
    支持 Windows，靠 x86/x64 的 PlatformTarget 区分）换成了 RuntimeIdentifier（Avalonia
    跨平台，发布时 -r <RID> 才是真正决定"要哪份原生库"的依据）。
    额外加一组"没有指定 RID 时按当前构建机器操作系统兜底"的判断，覆盖本地
    `dotnet run`/`dotnet build`（不带 -r）的日常开发场景——这组兜底判断等价于
    src/SevenZipLite/msbuild-targets/SevenZipLite.Native.targets 打进 NuGet 包里的那份，
    但这里是 ProjectReference 不是 PackageReference，那份包内 targets 不会自动生效，
    所以在本项目里单独复刻一份同样的兜底逻辑。

    下面覆盖了 win-x64/win-x86/win-arm64/linux-x64 四个 RID 分支，但本项目**正式支持并
    会被 CI 以 Native AOT 发布**的只有 win-x64 和 linux-x64——win-x86 分支只是为了让
    `dotnet run -r win-x86` / `dotnet build -r win-x86`（普通 JIT，不触发 PublishAot）
    这类本地调试场景也能顺手找到原生库，并不代表 win-x86 是一个受支持的 Native AOT 发布
    目标（.NET Native AOT 在 Windows 上只支持 x64/arm64，发布 win-x86 会直接报
    NETSDK1203，见上面 PublishAot 属性旁边的注释）；win-arm64 分支同理是预留，见
    native-libs/win-arm64/README.md 的说明。

    Native binary distribution strategy mirrors the old WPF demo (copy to the output
    root so [LibraryImport("7zlite")]'s default probing finds it), but the selection
    key changes from PlatformTarget (WPF is Windows-only, distinguishing x86/x64 via
    PlatformTarget) to RuntimeIdentifier (Avalonia is cross-platform; publishing with
    -r <RID> is what actually decides which native binary is needed). An extra "fall
    back to the current build machine's OS when no RID is specified" branch covers
    everyday local `dotnet run`/`dotnet build` (without -r) — equivalent to what
    src/SevenZipLite/msbuild-targets/SevenZipLite.Native.targets does when packed into
    the NuGet package, but since this project uses a ProjectReference rather than a
    PackageReference, that packed-in targets file doesn't automatically apply here, so
    the same fallback logic is reproduced locally in this project instead.

    The branches below cover win-x64/win-x86/win-arm64/linux-x64, but only win-x64 and
    linux-x64 are **officially supported and published as Native AOT by CI** — the
    win-x86 branch exists purely so local debugging scenarios like `dotnet run -r
    win-x86` / `dotnet build -r win-x86` (plain JIT, which doesn't trigger PublishAot)
    can still find the native library; it doesn't mean win-x86 is a supported Native
    AOT publish target (.NET Native AOT on Windows only supports x64/arm64 — publishing
    win-x86 fails outright with NETSDK1203, see the comment next to the PublishAot
    property above). The win-arm64 branch is likewise just a reservation for the
    future; see native-libs/win-arm64/README.md.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid Condition="'$(_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid)' == '' And '$(RuntimeIdentifier)' != ''">$(RuntimeIdentifier)</_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid>
    <_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid Condition="'$(_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid)' == '' And $([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows'))">win-x64</_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid>
    <_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid Condition="'$(_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid)' == '' And $([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Linux'))">linux-x64</_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid)' == 'win-x64' And Exists('..\..\native-libs\win-x64\7zlite.dll')">
    <None Include="..\..\native-libs\win-x64\7zlite.dll" Link="7zlite.dll" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid)' == 'win-x86' And Exists('..\..\native-libs\win-x86\7zlite.dll')">
    <None Include="..\..\native-libs\win-x86\7zlite.dll" Link="7zlite.dll" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid)' == 'win-arm64' And Exists('..\..\native-libs\win-arm64\7zlite.dll')">
    <None Include="..\..\native-libs\win-arm64\7zlite.dll" Link="7zlite.dll" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(_AvaloniaDemoNativeRid)' == 'linux-x64' And Exists('..\..\native-libs\linux-x64\lib7zlite.so')">
    <None Include="..\..\native-libs\linux-x64\lib7zlite.so" Link="lib7zlite.so" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
